# LoBBS command IoC

LoBBS is a stateless slash CLI over mesh DMs. **Plugins own verbs and filter lines.** The registry peels one verb and runs the bus. One wireup file lists plugins.

Player docs: [README.md](../../README.md). Bus behavior: [docs/lobbs-commands.md](../../docs/lobbs-commands.md).

## Required layout

| Layer | Role | May include |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `LoBBSDispatch.cpp` | Trim line, session/auth lookup, `lobbsCommandsHandle` | `LoBBSCommandRegistry.h`, `AuthDal` for session only |
| `LoBBSHooks.*` | `lobbsAddAction`, `lobbsAddFilter`, `lobbsDoAction`, `lobbsApplyFilter` (`std::vector` hooks) | No plugin or DAL headers |
| `LoBBSCommandRegistry.*` | Peel `/[id] verb`, arg cursor, pager, reply helpers | `LoBBSHooks.h` only (no `apps/*Commands.h`) |
| `LoBBSWireup.cpp` | `lobbsHooksReset()` + each `lobbs*RegisterCommands()` | All plugin `*Commands.h` |
| `apps/<App>/*Commands.*` | `slash_cmd` handler + filter callbacks | That app's DAL, `LoBBSHooks`, registry helpers |
| `apps/AppUtil.*` | Core auth directory (load user, username lookup) | Auth DAL internally |
| `apps/<App>/<App>.cpp` | Construct app / DAL wiring | No command switch |

## Session and core auth

- `LoBBSSession` on `LoBBSCommandCtx` (`nodeId`, `userUuid`, `username`, `isSysop`). Dispatch resolves it once via Auth.
- Registry helpers: `lobbsCtxLoggedIn`, `lobbsCtxUserUuid`, `lobbsCtxUsername`, `lobbsCommandRequireLogin`, `lobbsCommandRequireSysop`.
- Feature plugins must not `#include` `AuthDal.h`. Use session + `AppUtil`.

## Actions

- **`slash_cmd`**: `lobbsDoAction("slash_cmd", ctx, verb, rest)`. Every subscriber runs; compare `verb` and return silently if not yours. No claim flag. No central unknown-command reply.
- Dispatch sets `ctx.rest` to the mutable remainder; handlers use `lobbsArgShift`, `lobbsArgTakePage`, `lobbsArgRest`, `lobbsArgShiftMany`, and `lobbsArgShiftUint` / `lobbsTokIsUint` (full-token decimal, no `atoi` partial parse).

## Filters

- **`root_commands`**: query `nullptr`. Append **top-level verbs only** (`mail`, `users`, `ls`, …). No subcommand paths. Help and `/hi` page via `lobbsCommandReplyPagedLines`.
- **`command_help`**: query is help remainder (`mail`, `mail send`, `users find`). Append usage lines (including subcommand detail) when the query matches your topic; otherwise no-op. Help replies `No help for that.` if the vector is empty.
- **`status_lines`**: append one line each; `/status` pages the vector.

Priority constants: `LOBBS_HOOK_PRIORITY_HELP`, `_AUTH`, `_FEATURE`, `_STATUS` (lower runs first).

## Do

- Help plugin owns `/help` and `/hi` (same catalog). Status owns `/status` only (not `/hi`). Time plugin owns `/time`.
- `/time`: show clock; sysop passes Unix seconds to set RTC via `perhapsSetRTC(..., forceUpdate=true)`.
- Auth: `/login`, `/logout`, `/whoami`, `/passwd`, `/users` subs in Auth plugin.
- Fs verbs are top-level (`ls`, `cat`, …) with sysop gate inside handlers.
- Call `lobbsWireup()` once from `LoBBSModule` construction.

## Don't

- Central verb switch or `lobbsCommandsInstall` / capped hook tables.
- `#include` plugin headers from `LoBBSCommandRegistry.cpp` or `LoBBSHooks.cpp`.
- Pre-tokenize the full line into `argv` (breaks multi-word mail/news bodies).
- `help_index`, `help_topics`, `lobbsCommandTrySubHelp`, or `?` help tokens.

## New plugin checklist

1. `lobbsAddAction("slash_cmd", …)` with verb compare + arg cursor.
2. Filters: `root_commands`, `command_help`, `status_lines` as needed.
3. One `lobbsXRegisterCommands()` in `LoBBSWireup.cpp`.
